From e5edc71db452ad4eb50a975b757a97ab1d936a68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:33:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/88] VS Code colors headline levels as Emacs does with
 org-lsp.headlineLevelColors

Themes give every markup.heading scope one color, so each level of
headlines looked alike. The new setting (off by default) turns headline
and stars tokens with a level into the token type `outline`, whose looks
are the colors of Emacs's outline-N faces (function, variable, keyword,
comment, type, constant, builtin, string) without markup.heading. Done,
TODO, archived headlines and inline tasks carry no level and keep their
look. It is a type rather than a modifier because the modifiers already
fill the 32 bits of LSP's bitset; the server never sends it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
