From b3df01701047a404765acbcb75f4088fae563100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:39:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/88] Helix shows the agenda and capture, and picks answers
 from the code actions

Helix 25.07 opens the documents a server asks it to show but does not
announce window.showDocument, and answers window/showMessageRequest with
Method not found. editors/helix/languages.toml now sets show_document and
a new integration option, message_requests = false: a question's choices
then come first in the code actions (kind org.answer), and a rename with
a choice's key answers too. With either, a plain client gets the agenda,
capture, refile and the other commands that ask as code actions, and
scheduling, deadlines, tags, properties and effort in Org files.

The agenda's edits to a plain client's file go one at a time, each once
the client has reported the last, as Helix refused the ones made against
a version it had left behind. Code actions tell the server where the
cursor is for any client that runs commands from them, so filing a
capture goes back to where it started.

editors/helix/test/run.py runs the agenda and capture scenarios, reading
the buffers from what Helix tells the server; only column view, the date
prompt, the note buffer and follow mode stay excepted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
