From 0af0b0939d1ae819dca688e4c92db5460b04ee1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:16:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/88] A habit's graph shows its days on org-habit's
 backgrounds in Neovim, Vim, VS Code and Zed

The looks of a habit's days fell back on Neovim's diff groups, and
`DiffDelete` has no background in the default colorscheme, so overdue
days showed none; VS Code and Zed gave the days a foreground only. The
manifest now gives these looks the backgrounds of org-habit's faces,
light and dark, the `-future` ones included as looks of two modifiers
(`agendaHabit.ready.future`). Neovim and Vim define the groups with
them where no colorscheme group exists, VS Code draws them as
decorations with theme colors of its own, Zed's rules give them a
little transparent. The highlighting sample has an overdue habit and
one due today, and each editor's highlighting test checks the days.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
