From 12878a40f78a6d0ddbf6901dec3ff474a5001b35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:23:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/88] Zed gives the clocked entry's line in the agenda the
 background of org-agenda-clocking

Zed showed the line the clock runs on in bold. Its rules now give the
line's tokens the background of `secondary-selection`, which
`org-agenda-clocking` inherits, from the manifest. Zed lets no extension
highlight a line from edge to edge, so the background ends with the
text; the Zed page and its checks say so. The highlighting screenshots
check that the background shows in Zed's agenda.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
