From 53e8827438b5a1fa157f5bc69b9a683f066b3d46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:35:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/88] Headline levels follow org-n-level-faces and
 org-cycle-level-faces, and org-fontify-whole-heading-line colors their whole
 line

The level token of a headline is that of `org-get-level-face`: past
`org_n_level_faces` the looks start again from the first, or with
`org_cycle_level_faces` off the deeper levels keep the last; checked
against Emacs (`scripts/level_faces_reference.py`, `tests/level-faces`).
With `org_fontify_whole_heading_line`, the server sends the headlines'
lines in `org-lsp/lineHighlights` (`headline.levelN`), which Neovim
(`line_hl_group`), Vim (a sign without text) and VS Code (the colours
`org.headlineLevelNBackground`) draw to the edge of the window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
