From 14f87ed347a90b495b3de7da8ded1b58b46137fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:45:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/88] Lines a long line wraps into go on under the text, a
 headline's title or an item's text, as wrap-prefix has them

With `org-indent-mode`, Neovim and Vim line the wrapped part of a line
up with a headline's title (its stars and a space) and an item's text a
column after its bullet (`org-list-item-body-column`), as well as with
its own indentation ('breakindent' with `list:-1`); neither can repeat
the prefix before them. Zed and Helix, whose prefixes are inlay hints,
wrap under the prefix and the line's own indentation. VS Code and
Sublime Text indent wrapped lines by the text's own whitespace only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
