From c72d9d65aa23f63b8e598163df311d958895dd55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/88] Custom properties are hidden and shown again with
 org.custom.properties.toggle, in Neovim and Sublime Text

`org-toggle-custom-properties-visibility`, ported with the lines it
hides as Org finds them (`custom_property_lines`, checked against Emacs
by `scripts/custom_properties_reference.py` and
`scripts/fuzz-custom-props.py`), and `org_custom_properties`. The
command answers `{ "hiddenLines": { uri, lines } }` for a client that
announces `experimental.orgHiddenLines` (or sets `hidden_lines`), and
nothing hidden the next time. Neovim conceals the lines whole
(`conceal_lines`); Sublime Text folds each from the end of the line
before. Vim, VS Code, Zed and Helix cannot hide a line on its own, and
are told so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
