From 705056a980f333089b091e4a9942a3341ecc76cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:13:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/88] org-journal's keys work in the calendar, which C-c >
 opens on its own, and follow mode shows the day's entry

org.goto.calendar (org-goto-calendar) shows the date prompt's calendar
with no date asked for, on the day of the line's timestamp. The keys
org-journal adds to calendar-mode-map act on the day of its cursor:
j r and j d read or display its entry, ] and [ go to the next and
previous days with an entry, j n makes an entry for it, j m marks the
days again, j s f, j s F, j s w, j s m and j s y search. With
org_journal_follow_mode, ] and [ display the entry of the day they go
to. Recorded against Emacs and fuzzed; org-journal-enable-cache changes
nothing that can be seen, and is marked as not needed. The Vim plugin
names the calendar as the document of the commands run in it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
