Subject: [PATCH 21/88] The Zed runner logs a request before its answer, and
 fails fast instead of hanging

proxy.py passed each message on before writing it to the log, from two
threads, so an answer could be logged before its request. run.py then
dropped the answer and waited for it until every settle ran out: the
org-editing hang under load, and the rename timeouts in agenda-bulk and
agenda-entry-edits. The proxy now logs before it passes on, the log keeps
an early answer for its request, an unanswered request fails its step,
each scenario has a time budget, and a killed runner stops its Zed and
Xvfb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
