From a7843b53cdf21f403399328401a03c6c91212542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:19:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/88] Neovim's own hover shows an agenda entry highlighted,
 and K is left to it

vim.lsp.buf.hover() shows the server's Org text as Markdown, coloured
only with a tree-sitter parser for Org. The plugin now sends org-lsp's
Org hovers to its float, an Org buffer the server highlights, so K (or
any mapping to the hover) shows the entry as Org files look. The plugin
no longer maps K in the agenda, and keeps the server's K
(org.agenda.habits) off it; hover stays a mapping name for another key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
