 | ~<S-Tab>~ | ~global_cycle~     | ~org~           | Cycle the visibility of the whole file                  |
 | ~q~       | ~quit~             | ~agenda~        | Close the agenda                                        |
-| ~K~       | ~hover~            | ~agenda~        | Show the entry of the line in a float, highlighted      |
+| none      | ~hover~            | ~agenda~        | Show the entry of the line in a float, highlighted      |
 | ~g?~      | ~help~             | ~org~, ~agenda~ | Show the keys of the buffer in a window (~q~ closes it) |
 
+In the agenda, Neovim's own ~K~ (~vim.lsp.buf.hover()~) shows the entry
+of the line: the plugin shows Org text the server answers a hover with in
+a float highlighted as Org files are, rather than as Markdown. Emacs's ~K~
+(~org.agenda.habits~) has no key there; ~hover~ maps the same float to
+another key.
