From ad764af723cf6cfef557c2582d01a2c551137d73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:44:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/88] org-protocol URLs reach the editor with org-lsp through
 org-lsp protocol

Every server listens for org-protocol URLs on a socket of its own (a Unix
socket in a directory only the user may enter, a loopback port with a
token on Windows) and says so in the state directory. `org-lsp protocol
URL`, which the system runs for the scheme, hands the URL to the server
the user worked in last, skipping those that stopped; the server stores
the link (store-link), starts a capture with the URL's template and the
link's properties for %:link, %:description, %i and %a (capture), or shows
the file org_protocol_project_alist maps the page to (open-source), with
Emacs's messages. With no server, a link is kept for the next one, and the
editor of org_protocol_editor is started, whose server takes the capture
left for it.

Neovim, Vim, VS Code and Sublime Text run the capture as from its key when
the server asks (org-lsp/runCommand, experimental.orgRunCommand or the
option run_command); for other clients the server runs it and asks itself.
New settings: org_protocol_default_template_key, org_protocol_data_separator,
org_protocol_project_alist, org_protocol_editor and run_command.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
