+:CUSTOM_ID: org_protocol_project_alist
+:END:
+
+Where the files of ~org-protocol://open-source~ URLs are on this computer.
+Each has a ~name~, the ~base_url~ of the pages (with its last slash) and the
+~working_directory~ of their files (with its last slash, =~/= for the home
+directory), and may have an ~online_suffix~ taken off the URL (~.html~), a
+~working_suffix~ put on in its place (~.org~), and ~rewrites~, pairs of an
+Emacs regular expression on the URL, whose first group is taken out of it, and
+what goes after it, for a URL whose file is not there. The first whose
+~base_url~ the URL has is tried first.
+
+- Org's option :: ~org-protocol-project-alist~
+- Type :: object[]
+- Default :: ~[]~
+
+#+begin_src toml
+org_protocol_project_alist = []
+#+end_src
+
+*** org_protocol_editor
+:PROPERTIES:
+:CUSTOM_ID: org_protocol_editor
+:END:
+
+The editor ~org-lsp protocol~ starts when no org-lsp runs, as a command line
+(~code~, ~zed~, ~kitty nvim~): it opens ~org_default_notes_file~ in it, or the
+file of an ~open-source~ URL, and the org-lsp that starts there takes the URL,
+within two minutes. Read from the shared file only. Without it, a stored link
+is kept for the next org-lsp that starts, and a capture fails.
+
+- Type :: string
+- Default :: unset: none: a capture waits for an editor with org-lsp
+
 ** Clocking
 :PROPERTIES:
 :CUSTOM_ID: clocking
