From 84bb97774efdaf864e64516e0565672e83a9c6fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:45:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/88] install.sh protocol registers org-lsp for org-protocol
 URLs, and the docs say how to use them

`scripts/install.sh protocol` makes `org-lsp protocol %u` the handler of
the scheme: a desktop entry and xdg-mime (or mimeapps.list) on Linux, an
AppleScript applet declaring CFBundleURLTypes registered with lsregister
on macOS, the scheme under HKCU\Software\Classes on Windows; the last two
are not tested here. docs/org-protocol.org has the setup, the bookmarklets,
what each handler does, org_protocol_editor for each editor, how the
editor is found and what differs from Emacs; configuration.org,
protocol.org (org-lsp/runCommand, the state directory) and a decision in
development.org go with it, and the parity tables have org-protocol.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
