From f0cea9c2db83fe968aa65b4a2038531458a3d832 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:32:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/88] The server waits for no download or program, and trusts
 no link with options or paths

- Remote images are downloaded by curl on a thread of their own, 20 MB at most, into one file per URL; the preview comes in org-lsp/images once they are there (quiet for those a file opens with in Neovim, VS Code and Sublime Text).
- man, info, ctags and Graphviz's dot are stopped after 60 seconds, with what they started (src/process.rs); a shell: link's output shows its first 50 lines or 8000 characters.
- Following an id: link reads only the files the kept IDs say have it, and looks again when none does.
- A man: link that would give man an option is refused; org-protocol open-source shows no file outside the project's working directory (both written down as differences from Emacs).
- shell-quote-argument quotes for cmd on Windows as Emacs's w32 branch does.
- org-clock-save writes its file whole (temporary file renamed over it).
- A state directory too deep for a socket's name has the org-protocol socket in /tmp/org-lsp-UID, made for the user alone; a server that cannot listen says so.
- org-roam-extract-new-file-path is filled by org-capture-fill-template first, as org-roam fills it.
- A test that nothing is sent before initialized.

