From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:29:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/88] The parser goes over citations, inline code and diary
 timestamps once

A citation's search for a key, the name after src_ and call_ and the
closing parenthesis of a diary timestamp are remembered, as the other
searches for closers are, so that many openers in a line are not each
scanned to its end. plain_link_end asked within a character finds no
link instead of panicking.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
