From 0ef684c5f02487abd9698e11583772f153db5dee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:10:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 45/88] The Helix and Zed checks name the routes they have, and
 the areas what they lack
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TESTING.org gave every check in Zed and Helix as "the code action /TITLE/".
The generator now knows what each has: Helix the code actions the server
offers a client without org-lsp's keys (`code_actions_at`, in Org files,
capture buffers and on agenda lines), Zed the keys of its keymap.json
(tasks) and the same code actions outside the agenda, both go to
definition for following links (`gd`, `F12`; `enter` and `tab` in Zed's
agenda). A check with a command neither runs is listed under "Not in
EDITOR" with what it lacks, not as a box to tick.

The areas say so: Table formulas, Encryption (both), Refile and archive
and Code blocks (Zed) are partly there now, and the other partial areas
name the commands left out (deleting properties, removing dates, IDs,
numbering, appointments, keyword sets, org-roam's and org-journal's,
BibTeX's…).

docs/vim.org asks for Vim 9.0.1485, as the plugin does; docs/sublime.org
says wrapped lines are indented by their own leading whitespace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
