From f485f49915a414469efc297880a6a5c02f2af518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:25:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/88] Test runners and scripts clean up after themselves and
 fail clearly

- VS Code: the outline path request (`agendaCursor`) has a rejection
  handler; the commands kept for the tests are the last 100, with a count
  of all, which the scenarios read.
- VS Code's runner removes each scenario run's folder and VS Code state.
- Zed's runner closes its copy of zed.log once Zed has it.
- Vim's runner quotes each word of the command tmux runs.
- ORG_LSP_E2E naming no scenario fails, not passes with nothing run.
- The inline task, numbering and startup alignment reference scripts give
  Emacs a timeout, as the others do.
- highlight-screenshots.py takes Zed's grammar from ZED_ORG_GRAMMAR (or
  ZED_TREE_SITTER_ORG) and says so when neither is set, not a path of one
  machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
