From ce535ea83d506e75f021d9fdc497d23b1bf7aa66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:08:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/88] One version everywhere, and the Zed and Sublime Text
 packages download their own release's server

scripts/version.sh X.Y.Z sets the version in the server's workspace
(Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock), the VS Code extension (package.json,
package-lock.json), the Zed extension (extension.toml, Cargo.toml,
Cargo.lock) and the Sublime Text package (VERSION in plugin.py); alone,
it prints it and fails when they disagree, which check.sh checks.

The Zed extension downloads the server of `v` and its crate's version,
or of ORG_LSP_RELEASE when it is built; the Sublime Text package, of
`'v' + VERSION`. The nightly build sets them to `nightly` (the Zed
extension built with ORG_LSP_RELEASE, the Sublime Text package's line
replaced), so it downloads the nightly server as before, and checks that
the extension names the release it should. A version tag that is not
`v` and the version fails before anything is built.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
