From f80c7271dde6b9621f0c20d1597d52377d4ed6e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:23:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 59/88] docs/emacs-options.org: every option emacs_options
 takes, with Org's documentation

A page with a heading for each of the 480 options Emacs reads, by the
file of Org it is in, written by scripts/generate-docs.mjs from
scripts/emacs-options.json: Org's docstring as Org (`foo' as ~foo~, what
Org would read as markup as code, lines laid out by hand in example
blocks), its default, its type, the version it came in, and its default
in the shared file where TOML can say it. Each heading's CUSTOM_ID is
GitHub's anchor of it, so the site's search finds each option and a link
reaches it. The generator fails when the recorded options are not those
marked `emacs`. The page is in the sidebar after Configuration; the
docs of `emacs_options` point to it instead of parity.org.

The schema of `emacs_options` names each option with the first sentence
of its docstring, its default and, where its type is simple, what it
takes, and no others, so VS Code's settings.json completes and describes
them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
