+*** org-html-text-markup-alist
+:PROPERTIES:
+:CUSTOM_ID: org-html-text-markup-alist
+:END:
+
+Alist of HTML expressions to convert text markup.
+
+The key must be a symbol among ~bold~, ~code~, ~italic~,
+~strike-through~, ~underline~ and ~verbatim~.  The value is
+a formatting string to wrap fontified text with.
+
+If no association can be found for a given markup, text will be
+returned as-is.
+
+- Default ::
+  #+begin_src emacs-lisp
+  ((bold . "<b>%s</b>")
+   (code . "<code>%s</code>")
+   (italic . "<i>%s</i>")
+   (strike-through . "<del>%s</del>")
+   (underline . "<span class=\"underline\">%s</span>")
+   (verbatim . "<code>%s</code>"))
+  #+end_src
+- Type ::
+  #+begin_src emacs-lisp
+  (alist :key-type
+         (symbol :tag "Markup type")
+         :value-type
+         (string :tag "Format string"))
+  #+end_src
+- Since :: Org 8.0
+
+#+begin_src toml
+[emacs_options]
+org-html-text-markup-alist = { bold = "<b>%s</b>", code = "<code>%s</code>", italic = "<i>%s</i>", strike-through = "<del>%s</del>", underline = "<span class=\"underline\">%s</span>", verbatim = "<code>%s</code>" }
+#+end_src
