+
+Non-nil means process LaTeX math snippets.
+
+When set, the exporter will process LaTeX environments and
+fragments.
+
+This option can also be set with the +OPTIONS line,
+e.g. "tex:dvipng".  Allowed values are:
+
+#+begin_example
+nil            Ignore math snippets.
+#+end_example
+
+t, ~mathml~    Convert the LaTeX fragments to MathML if the
+
+#+begin_example
+               `org-latex-to-mathml-convert-command' is usable.
+SYMBOL         Convert the LaTeX fragments to images using any symbol
+               defined in `org-preview-latex-process-alist', e.g.,
+               `dvipng'.
+`verbatim'     Keep everything in verbatim.
+#+end_example
+
+If the desired converter is not available or any other symbol is
+provided, process as ~verbatim~.
+
+- Default :: ~t~
+- Type ::
+  #+begin_src emacs-lisp
+  (choice
+   (const :tag "Do not process math in any way" nil)
+   (choice :tag "Convert fragments to MathML" :value t
+           (const t)
+           (const mathml))
+   (restricted-sexp :tag "Convert fragments to images" :value dvipng :match-alternatives
+                    ((closure
+                         (hfy-user-sheet-assoc hfy-html-quote-regex hfy-html-quote-map hfy-face-to-css hfy-begin-span-handler hfy-end-span-handler archive-zip-extract nxml-auto-insert-xml-declaration-flag t)
+                         (v)
+                       (assq v org-preview-latex-process-alist))))
+   (const :tag "Leave math verbatim" verbatim))
+  #+end_src
+- Since :: Org 9.8
+
+#+begin_src toml
+[emacs_options]
+org-odt-with-latex = true
+#+end_src
